```
===================================================================
Detection Name: Password Spraying & Brute Force Detection
Author: SOC Team
Data Source: index=wineventlog (Windows Security Event Logs)
Event ID: 4625 (An account failed to log on)
MITRE ATT&CK: T1110 (Brute Force / Password Spraying)
Severity: High
Threshold: 10 or more failed logon attempts from the same source IP 
           or against multiple targets within a 15-minute window
False Positives: 
  - Misconfigured service accounts with expired passwords
  - Vulnerability scanners / authorized penetration tests
Recommended Action:
  1. Correlate with subsequent Event 4624 (Logon Type 3) to identify 
     if the attacker successfully authenticated.
  2. Inspect source IP on threat intelligence (AbuseIPDB, VirusTotal).
  3. If external or untrusted source, enforce temporary IP block on firewall.
===================================================================
```
index=wineventlog EventCode=4625 
| stats count by src_ip, TargetUserName 
| where count >= 10
| sort - count
